Individual authors retain copyright in their contributions.

This repository contains separately licensed components. It is not offered
under a choice of MIT or GPL for every file.

Scope (paths are relative to the repository root):

* Server/**, Server.MirForms/** and Tests/**: GNU General Public License,
  version 3 only (SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only).
  The full licence text is in LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt.
* Client/** and Shared/**: MIT (SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT).
  The full licence text is in LICENSE-MIT.txt.
* Other original Crystal source code, tools, build files and documentation:
  MIT, unless an explicit file or component notice states otherwise.

These defaults cover project-authored material only. Third-party code,
packages, bundled libraries and assets retain their own terms. Existing
third-party copyright and licence notices take precedence for that material.
This notice does not grant rights in third-party game artwork, sounds, maps,
trademarks or other content. See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

MIT-licensed shared code remains available under MIT when used separately.
A combined server work containing GPL-covered code must be distributed in
compliance with GPL v3, including preservation of applicable MIT notices.
Moving GPL-covered code to a different directory does not change its licence.

The server is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it under
the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the Free Software
Foundation, version 3 of the License only.

The server is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY
WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR
A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt for details.

Historical releases and contributions
-------------------------------------

The initial repository commit (21afcf15) included GPL v2 licence text; that
file was removed in commit 355595f1. A GPL v2 badge was subsequently added to
the README in commit 2ca18a9b. This notice does not revoke rights validly
granted for earlier versions or determine the licence of every historical
contribution. The sample 'or later' wording inside a licence's application
instructions does not itself establish a project-specific grant.

These terms grant only rights that the relevant copyright holders are
authorized to grant. Relicensing another contributor's work requires their
permission or an existing licence that permits the change. This notice does
not establish that such permission has been obtained or override incompatible
existing terms. Maintainers must verify the necessary permissions before
publishing the existing codebase under this split licensing arrangement.
